7. How to run it

1. Import/boot the Ubuntu VM on an internal-only VirtualBox network (no NAT/bridged adapter attached).
2. Set the static IP to `192.168.50.10/24` via netplan, with `ipv4.never-default: true`.
3. From the VM:
   ```bash
   python3 clinic_app.py
   ```
4. Browse to `http://192.168.50.10:8000` from a machine on the same internal network.

8. Why this setup

- Host-only/internal networking with no default route guarantees nothing done to this app — including exploitation later in the project — can reach the real internet or any other host.
- A pure-Python app with no external dependencies keeps the attack surface simple and fully understood, which matters for the log-analysis and hardening tasks coming next.
- A snapshot before any attack work** means the environment can always be returned to a known-good baseline, so testing is repeatable and safe.
